should be able to:
    - start new process from other bin
    - redirect output process using PIPE
    - keep ansi sequence (color, hyperlink, ...)
    - remove duplicate
    - internal communication client <-> server (ipc)
    - contact ollama through socket TCP localhost (failsafe)

parameters:
    [global]
    - help
    - verbose mode

    [special mode]
    - mode to install ollama
    - mode to setup a user daemon

    [client mode]
    - process to start
    - forge rules from .cfg

    [server mode]
    - ip ollama
    - port ollama
    - model used
    - system-prompt used

usages:
    [global]
    context-forge -h

    [special mode]
    context-forge setup
    context-forge remove
    context-forge install-ollama

    [client mode]
    context-forge exec [-v|--verbose <level>] <command> [<args>]*

    [server mode]
    context-forge server (-r|--rules <cfg_path>)* [-ip <ollama_ip>] [-p|--port <ollama_port>] [-m|--model <model_name>] [-s|--system-prompt <system-prompt_path>] [-v|--verbose <level>]
